course: dictionary
lesson: 2689
title: What does diet mean?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word diet has more than one meaning, so look at the words around it. «A balanced diet is a mix of foods from all the food groups.» Here diet means all the food and drink you usually have, not a plan to lose weight.
explain: Diet can also mean a special plan of eating, often for health. «Children do not need diets unless a doctor says so» shows that a diet is something a doctor might choose for a reason, not something to try for fun.
explain: Animals have diets too. The diet of an animal is what it naturally eats: a panda's diet is mostly bamboo. Always check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Your diet is all the food and drink you usually have.
fact: A diet can also be a special plan of eating, for health or to lose weight.
fact: The diet of an animal is what it naturally eats. Herbivores eat plants, carnivores eat meat, and omnivores eat both.
fact: «A balanced diet is a mix of foods from all the food groups.»
fact: «Diet» drinks use sweeteners with almost no sugar.
exercise: «A balanced diet is a mix of foods from all the food groups.» What does diet mean here? | A place where animals live | Exercise you do at the gym | A plan to lose weight quickly | *All the food and drink you usually have
exercise: «Children do not need diets unless a doctor says so.» Which meaning of diet fits? | The sound a dog makes | *A special plan of eating, chosen for health | A type of sweet snack | Something you eat only on birthdays
exercise: What does the diet of an animal mean? | The colour of its fur | Where it sleeps at night | How fast it can run | *What it naturally eats
test: «Diet drinks use sweeteners with almost no sugar.» What does diet mean in diet drink? | A drink you must share | *A drink made with sweeteners and almost no sugar | A drink with lots of sugar | A hot drink for breakfast
test: Which word means to eat less or eat certain foods to lose weight? | *dieting | grazing | feasting | balancing
exam: An omnivore eats both plants and meat. Which words describe an omnivore's diet? | Only meat | Only plants | Only water | *Both plants and meat
